---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SHIPPING, DELIVERY } from '../lib/library';

const tables = [
  { title: 'Keyrings, fridge magnets and sets', rows: SHIPPING['free-ireland'].rows },
  { title: 'Lamps, plaques, keepsakes and most other pieces', rows: SHIPPING.included.rows },
  { title: 'Christmas baubles', rows: SHIPPING['free-everywhere'].rows },
  { title: 'Large signs', rows: SHIPPING.standard.rows },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Delivery and Returns"
  description="Free collection in Dublin, free hand delivery in the Dublin area on orders of €100 or more, postage across Ireland, the EU and worldwide, delivery times and returns."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Delivery and returns', href: '/delivery-and-returns/' }]} />
    <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl sm:text-4xl mb-8">Delivery and returns</h1>

    <div class="product-body text-paper/75 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-paper">Collection in Dublin</h2>
      <p>Free collection in {DELIVERY.collectionAreas}, by arrangement. We agree the time and the place by email when your order is ready.</p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-paper pt-4">Hand delivery in Dublin</h2>
      <p>
        Orders of €{DELIVERY.handDeliveryMin} or more get free hand delivery in {DELIVERY.handDeliveryArea}.
        Outside the Dublin area, for example Naas, orders go by post.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-paper pt-4">Postage</h2>
      <p>
        Postage works in four ways, depending on the piece. The product page shows the one that applies,
        and the tables below list all four.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Keyrings, fridge magnets and sets:</strong> the price is the same everywhere. Delivery in Ireland is free. For the EU, the first item adds the postage shown and each extra item in the same order adds the smaller amount.</li>
        <li><strong>Lamps, plaques, keepsakes and most other pieces:</strong> delivery in Ireland is built into the price, so there is nothing to add. Buyers in the EU and the UK pay a little more on the price, and buyers in the US a little more again, instead of a separate postage charge.</li>
        <li><strong>Christmas baubles:</strong> one price, with free delivery in Ireland, the EU and the US.</li>
        <li><strong>Large signs:</strong> postage is added to the price. The first item costs the postage shown and each extra item in the same order adds the smaller amount.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mt-5">
      {tables.map((t) => (
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-paper/10 p-5">
          <h3 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-gold mb-3">{t.title}</h3>
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <tbody>
              {t.rows.map((row) => (
                <tr class="border-b border-paper/10 last:border-0">
                  <th scope="row" class="text-left font-normal text-paper/70 py-2">{row.region}</th>
                  <td class="text-right py-2">
                    <span class="font-semibold">{row.price}</span>
                    {'extra' in row && row.extra && <span class="block text-xs text-paper/55">+{row.extra} each extra item</span>}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="product-body text-paper/75 leading-relaxed space-y-4 mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-paper">Delivery times</h2>
      <p>Estimated time from when you confirm your order until it arrives:</p>
      <ul>
        {DELIVERY.times.map((t) => <li>{t.region}: {t.days}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p>
        It depends on the piece, how complex it is and the personalisation, so I confirm the timing in my first reply.
        Custom pieces that I design for you take longer, and I give you their timing together with the price.
      </p>
      <p>Larger items go with tracking. Keyrings, magnets, sets and other small flat pieces (like the dachshund ruler and the comb) go by An Post letter or large envelope, without tracking.</p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-paper pt-4">Customs and import duties</h2>
      <p>
        Everything is posted from Ireland, so buyers in the EU pay no customs fees.
        Outside the EU, import duties and taxes are set by your country and paid by you on delivery.
        Before I post an order outside the EU, I message you an estimate and only ship once you agree.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-paper pt-4">Returns</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Personalised items:</strong> each one is made with your name, text or details, so it can't be returned or exchanged,
          unless it arrives damaged or faulty.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Items that aren't personalised</strong>, for example the barber pole lamp or the lanterns: you can cancel within 14 days of receiving them.
          Email me first and send the item back in the same condition. You pay the return postage, and I refund what you paid, including the original postage.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Damaged or not what we agreed:</strong> email me a photo within 14 days of receiving it and I'll remake it or refund you.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>None of this affects your legal rights as a consumer. Orders placed on Etsy follow Etsy's own policies and Purchase Protection.</p>

      <p class="pt-4">Questions? Email <a href="mailto:contact@make3d.ie">contact@make3d.ie</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
